---
description: Automatic review, clean-code and documentation checkpoints after coding turns
alwaysApply: true
---

User-level hooks for Claude Code, Cursor and Codex start a background quality checkpoint after a turn ends. It is described in `docs/quality-checkpoints.md`.
- A git-based gate skips insignificant changes.
- A model triage then decides between a clean-code pass, a documentation pass, both or neither.
- The result is auto-applied to the working tree. Nothing is staged or committed.

Nothing needs to be run after each turn. If a prompt arrives with a "Quality worker … applied edits to …" notice, re-read those files before editing them.
Run `pnpm finish-work` only to force a checkpoint now (for example before leaving); add `--actions clean,docs` to skip triage.
To inspect status, runs or patches, follow `.cursor/rules/quality-inspect-and-run.mdc`.
When `AGENT_QUALITY_CHILD=1`, you are inside a checkpoint: follow the stage prompt and never run finish-work or start another worker.
